      "message": "I had originally used `https` instead of `http`, but tests fail for a reason that I don\u0027t understand. Updating this to prepend `https://` and updating the rewriting logic in the tests to prepend `https://` gets:\n```\n ❌ gr-formatted-text tests \u003e as markdown \u003e does default linking\n      AssertionError: expected \u0027http://www.google.com\u0027 to equal \u0027https://www.google.com\u0027\n      + expected - actual\n\n      -http://www.google.com\n      +https://www.google.com\n\n      at checkLinking (polygerrit-ui/app/elements/shared/gr-formatted-text/gr-formatted-text_test.ts:781:15)\n      at async Ka.\u003canonymous\u003e (polygerrit-ui/app/elements/shared/gr-formatted-text/gr-formatted-text_test.ts:793:6)\n```\n\nThis is for the `await checkLinking(\u0027www.google.com\u0027);` case which doesn\u0027t have a scheme and should be getting rewritten with `https://`, but it doesn\u0027t.\n\nIf you mean using `link: \u0027//$1\u0027`, that gets:\n```\n ❌ gr-formatted-text tests \u003e as markdown \u003e does default linking\n      AssertionError: expected \u0027http://www.google.com\u0027 to equal \u0027//www.google.com\u0027\n      + expected - actual\n\n      -http://www.google.com\n      +//www.google.com\n\n      at checkLinking (polygerrit-ui/app/elements/shared/gr-formatted-text/gr-formatted-text_test.ts:781:15)\n      at async Ka.\u003canonymous\u003e (polygerrit-ui/app/elements/shared/gr-formatted-text/gr-formatted-text_test.ts:793:6)\n```\n\nThis is also failing `await checkLinking(\u0027www.google.com\u0027);` case. Like the other attempt, `www.google.com` is schemeless and the text expects it to get rewritten to `//www.google.com`, but it\u0027s rewritten to `http://google.com`.\n\n@milutin@google.com let me know what I\u0027m missing. Do you know why it keeps on rewriting with `http://`?",
